    "text": "# Independent no-data CDP repair review\n\nThe one-file test producer patch SHA-256 `e761d493f198abdb2e817deb62d0e253fe0ba5a53a003cf5c6a896113f3dd3a6` is supported within its bounded no-data probe scope. It applies cleanly at canonical `b27a11f9ad7edbbb9484659d2ab430bd16ec545c`; preimage SHA-256 `4c49b5e20554da1771350b81fb2921f1de2ce294a79877679f5e78f8e210fc58` and isolated afterimage `ddeceabd18cbe49af0730eb08448c4cf2bf823ac0bb2034300455561425a75bb` match. The patch replaces only browser launch, server and DOM-result retrieval, preserving subject selection, all observation comparisons, source/type assertions, variants and fault controls.\n\nThe owned helper is used with ephemeral debug port and required announced endpoint; its existing lifecycle checks authenticate the endpoint and require cleanup. Polling the report's actual `textContent` retains error and timeout handling while avoiding HTML entity re-decoding. The prior direct dump-dom attempt retained a 20-second timeout; its cause is not established.\n\nThe actual retained report SHA-256 `4017219e035402f3cdb4d56e589e8d16334cb8ea02b6cd43f1d3201e41035136` records original, MAIN and 21.x source models, seven DOM/lifecycle cases each, and six rejected fault variants. The run manifest SHA-256 `909242c120ee33f60d61d1eda9aedde61ab282b8ed7f7ddc0703bbdec907194f` records the exact command, zero exit, Node 24.21, pinned ARM Chromium 149 and isolated copied probe; report, log and recorded binary hashes match. Tool version and hash checks were recorded after execution, and this particular run did not query browser sandbox state. Inputs outside the copied probe are symlinked to the canonical source tree by convention. No browser rerun by this reviewer.\n\nThe observed renderer and view/outlet machinery are replayed with explicit protocols; this is not a complete CdkTable, actual compiled owned node, packed application, browser/floor matrix, source-proof admission, security or G11 qualification. No canonical files were changed.\n"
  },
